*.go text eol=lf

# The vendored CLI is a ~10 MB binary that git cannot delta-compress: every
# vendoring adds another full copy to the history, permanently. Measured on
# 2026-09-20: 8 distinct blobs, .git at 44 MB, roughly 86% of the repository.
#
# LFS stores a ~130 byte pointer in the commit and keeps the binary outside the
# object database, so a clone fetches only the current version instead of all
# eight.
#
# This stops future growth only. The eight blobs already in the history stay
# where they are: removing them means rewriting history, which invalidates every
# existing clone and every commit hash the server and CI refer to. That is a
# separate decision, not a side effect of this one.
#
# Anyone checking out this repository needs git-lfs installed, and CI must
# checkout with lfs: true — without it the build receives the pointer file and
# tries to execute 130 bytes of text as a binary.
bin/grants-pp-cli-linux filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text